Imagine you’re at a traffic light. You don’t just drive blindly—you check the color and decide:
- Green? Go!
- Yellow? Slow down.
- Red? Stop!

Selections work the same way in code. They let your program check conditions and pick the right path.

• **Basic `if` statement**: Do something only if a condition is true
  ```java
  if (hungry) {
      eatSnack();
  }
  ```

• **`if-else`**: Choose between two options
  ```java
  if (raining) {
      takeUmbrella();
  } else {
      wearSunglasses();
  }
  ```

• **Multiple conditions**: Handle more complex decisions
  ```java
  if (temperature > 30) {
      System.out.println("Hot!");
  } else if (temperature > 20) {
      System.out.println("Warm");
  } else {
      System.out.println("Cold");
  }
  ```

